        "title": "Raw Materials - Silica Sand, Soda Ash, Cullet, Colorants",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Glass batch is deceptively simple: mostly sand, some soda ash, some limestone, plus cullet (recycled glass). The complexity is in the specifications. Iron contamination in silica sand determines whether you get colorless or green glass. The ratio of batch-to-cullet affects energy consumption. The colorants you choose determine what light the glass transmits and absorbs."
